'''Zaralek Cavern''' is an enormous cave system underneath the [[Dragon Isles]]. It is accessed via a large cave between the [[Ohn'ahran Plains]] and [[Valdrakken]].

Deep beneath the [[Obsidian Citadel]] from which Neltharion once defended the Dragon Isles lies a vast hidden laboratory where the [[Neltharion|Earth-Warder]] conducted experiments... forbidden practices he wanted to conceal from the [[Dragon Aspects|other Aspects]]. Within these halls lies the shadow chamber from which Neltharion first communed with the [[Old God]]s, walking a path that would one day lead to his transformation into Deathwing.

While [[Raszageth]] has been defeated, the [[Primalists]] carry on in their bid to unravel all the [[titan]]s have wrought and must forge new alliances–or rekindle old ones. As the [[Adventurer|heroes]] of [[Azeroth]] pursue enemies into the dangers of Zaralek Cavern, they are aided by the local inhabitants found under the Dragon Isles — the molefolk known as [[Niffen]] and the [[Drogbar]]. They may not know much of the surface wars, but their knowledge of the underground is key to players and their allies finding their footing within.

==Getting there==
[[File:Iridikron's Gambit exterior.jpg|thumb|The exterior of Iridikron's Gambit]]
To reach the cavern, complete the first few quests of the [[Embers of Neltharion campaign]], then dragonride into [[Iridikron's Gambit]], the large cave mouth at {{co|89|29|Ohn'ahran Plains}} in the [[Cascades Canyon]] between the [[Ohn'ahran Plains]] and [[Petitioner's Concourse]] of [[Thaldraszus]] and [[Valdrakken]].

There are three flight paths within the cavern: at [[Loamm]], [[Dragonscale Camp]], and [[Obsidian Rest]]. The flight paths connect to the surface of the [[Dragon Isles]] by clicking the "Dragon Isles" corner of the map.

Two additional paths are also open at the start: the [[Old Loamm Road]] tunnel from [[Teerakai]] at {{co|36|59|Ohn'ahran Plains}} in southwestern Ohn'ahran Plains, and the [[Lookout Breach]] tunnel from [[Three-Falls Lookout]] at {{co|19|23|Azure Span}} in northwestern [[Azure Span]]. Both tunnels connect to [[Warder's Teeth]] in southwestern Zaralek Cavern.

